0..37 Comment "// This source defines a precategory."
38..40 Comment "//"
41..117 Comment "// `CatShape` has objects, a dependent hom type, identities and composition."
118..171 Comment "// Its unit and associativity laws are rewrite rules."
172..174 Comment "//"
175..252 Comment "// `SetoidCat` models the shape with types and functions. It checks every law"
253..318 Comment "// by conversion. One law can prove another law of the same type."
319..321 Comment "//"
322..352 Comment "// - see: #1510 — `CatShape`"
353..413 Comment "// - see: #452 — `identity_observed`, `composite_observed`"
414..437 Comment "// - cites: [HoTT-Book]"
438..440 Comment "//"
441..589 Comment "// [HoTT-Book]: https://homotopytypetheory.org/book/ \"The Univalent Foundations Program, Homotopy Type Theory: Univalent Foundations of Mathematics\""
591..667 Comment "/// `CatShape` defines a morphism sort indexed by two objects. It reads each"
668..726 Comment "/// law at the composite\'s objects, so the unit laws agree"
727..755 Comment "/// at `comp(id(a), id(a))`."
